(>> Example 3.1: ETAP Power Flow and Shunt Capacitor Sizing) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Statement: A 33 kV utility substation supplies power to a remote manufacturing cluster) Tj
T*
(over an 8 km, 3-phase radial distribution feeder. Feeder parameters and load conditions) Tj
T*
(are:) Tj
T*
(- Line Impedance: Z_line = \(0.32 + j 0.58\) Ohms per km) Tj
T*
(- Connected Industrial Load: S_load = 12 MVA at a lagging power factor of 0.80) Tj
T*
(- Substation Sending End Bus Voltage: V_s = 33.0 kV \(line-to-line\)) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Calculate the total feeder loop impedance, load current, and receiving end) Tj
T*
(line-to-line bus voltage \(V_r\) without compensation.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Calculate the feeder percentage voltage regulation and total active power) Tj
T*
(transmission loss \(kW\).) Tj
T*
(\(c\) Determine the rating of a shunt capacitor bank \(MVAR\) required at the receiving bus) Tj
T*
(to boost the power factor to 0.96 lagging and restore V_r to nominal 33 kV.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Solution:) Tj
T*
(1. Feeder Total Impedance and Receiving Load Current:) Tj
T*
(- Total resistance: R_total = 0.32 * 8 = 2.56 Ohms) Tj
T*
(- Total inductive reactance: X_total = 0.58 * 8 = 4.64 Ohms) Tj
T*
(- Total feeder impedance: Z_line = \(2.56 + j 4.64\) Ohms \(|Z| = sqrt\(2.56^2 + 4.64^2\) =) Tj
T*
(5.297 Ohms\).) Tj
T*
(- Load active and reactive power:) Tj
T*
(P_load = S_load * cos\(Phi\) = 12 * 0.80 = 9.60 MW = 9,600 kW) Tj
T*
ET

