(Step-by-Step Solution:) Tj
T*
(1. Calculation of Duty Cycle \(D\):) Tj
T*
(- Neglecting diode and switch conduction drops: D = V_out / V_in = 12.0 / 48.0 = 0.25) Tj
T*
(\(25.0%\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Sizing the Power Inductor \(L\):) Tj
T*
(- Permissible inductor ripple current: Delta_I_L = 0.20 * 15.0 A = 3.0 A.) Tj
T*
(- Inductor volt-second balance: V_L = L * \(Delta_I_L / Delta_t\) = \(V_in - V_out\)) Tj
T*
(- Since Delta_t = D * T_sw = D / f_sw:) Tj
T*
(L = [ \(V_in - V_out\) * D ] / \(f_sw * Delta_I_L\)) Tj
T*
(L = [ \(48.0 - 12.0\) * 0.25 ] / \(100,000 * 3.0\) = [ 36.0 * 0.25 ] / 300,000 = 9.0 /) Tj
T*
(300,000 = 30.0 microHenries.) Tj
T*
(- Standard E-series selection: 33 microH, 20 A saturation current shielded power) Tj
T*
(inductor.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Sizing the Output Filter Capacitor \(C\):) Tj
T*
(- In a buck converter, the inductor ripple current flows entirely into the output) Tj
T*
(capacitor:) Tj
T*
(Delta_V_out = Delta_I_L / \(8 * f_sw * C\)) Tj
T*
(C = Delta_I_L / \(8 * f_sw * Delta_V_out\)) Tj
T*
(- Given Delta_V_out = 0.01 * 12.0 = 0.12 V:) Tj
T*
(C = 3.0 / \(8 * 100,000 * 0.12\) = 3.0 / 96,000 = 31.25 microFarads.) Tj
T*
(- Accounting for ceramic capacitor DC-bias capacitance degradation \(40% loss at 12V DC\):) Tj
T*
(C_actual = 31.25 / 0.60 = 52.08 microF. Select four 22 microF, 25V X7R ceramic) Tj
T*
(capacitors in parallel \(88 microF total\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Discrete PI Controller Discretization \(Tustin Transform\):) Tj
T*
(- Continuous PI controller: G_c\(s\) = K_p + \(K_i / s\)) Tj
T*
(- Sampling time T_s chosen equal to switching period T_sw = 10 microseconds \(100 kHz) Tj
T*
(sampling\).) Tj
T*
(- Tustin substitution: s = \(2 / T_s\) * \( \(1 - z^-1\) / \(1 + z^-1\) \)) Tj
T*
(- G_c\(z\) = K_p + K_i * \(T_s / 2\) * \( \(1 + z^-1\) / \(1 - z^-1\) \)) Tj
T*
(- Numerical values: K_p = 1.8; K_i * \(T_s / 2\) = 850 * \(10 * 10^-6 / 2\) = 850 * 5 *) Tj
T*
(10^-6 = 0.00425.) Tj
T*
(- G_c\(z\) = [ \(1.8 + 0.00425\) - \(1.8 - 0.00425\) * z^-1 ] / [ 1 - z^-1 ]) Tj
T*
(- Difference Equation for DSP implementation:) Tj
T*
(u[n] = u[n-1] + 1.80425 * e[n] - 1.79575 * e[n-1], where e[n] is the voltage error.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> Example 3.3: Formula Student Electric EV Accumulator Pack Design) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Statement: A student racing team participating in Formula Bharat Electric is designing a) Tj
T*
(400 V nominal lithium-ion accumulator container complying with FSAE electric vehicle) Tj
T*
(regulations:) Tj
T*
(- Lithium-ion Cell: High-discharge 21700 cylindrical cells \(Molicel P42A\)) Tj
T*
(- Nominal cell voltage: V_cell = 3.60 V \(Fully charged = 4.20 V, Cut-off = 3.00 V\)) Tj
T*
