(>> Example 3.4: High-Voltage PCB Creepage & Clearance Sizing \(IEC 60664-1\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Statement: A power electronics engineer is laying out the printed circuit board for an) Tj
T*
(off-grid solar inverter operating with an internal DC bus voltage of 600 V DC and rated) Tj
T*
(impulse withstand voltage of 4.0 kV.) Tj
T*
(- Environmental Conditions: Pollution Degree 2 \(standard industrial laboratory) Tj
T*
(environment\)) Tj
T*
(- PCB Substrate Material: FR-4 fiberglass \(Comparative Tracking Index CTI = 175 V to 400) Tj
T*
(V, Material Group IIIa\)) Tj
T*
(- Insulation Requirement: Reinforced / Double Isolation between high-voltage DC bus and) Tj
T*
(low-voltage microcontroller logic.) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Determine the minimum clearance distance \(through air\) according to IEC 60664-1.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Determine the minimum creepage distance \(along the PCB surface\) for basic and) Tj
T*
(reinforced insulation.) Tj
T*
(\(c\) If space constraints restrict creepage to 4.0 mm, design an isolation milling slot) Tj
T*
(to satisfy safety requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Solution:) Tj
T*
(1. Minimum Clearance Distance Determination \(IEC 60664-1 Table F.2\):) Tj
T*
(- Clearance is determined by the impulse withstand voltage \(peak voltage transient\):) Tj
T*
(- For an impulse withstand rating of 4.0 kV in an inhomogeneous electric field \(Case B\):) Tj
T*
